0..77 Comment "// A hold at grade one. `hold[1] c = e;` holds a value no one else holds: the"
78..155 Comment "// value is made where the hold stands, and it is never copied while held. An"
156..231 Comment "// exclusive access moves the value out to its view, the view is read once,"
232..310 Comment "// and `resume` writes the new value back, so the write-back needs no count of"
311..389 Comment "// the value\'s other holders. `hold c = e;` holds at the default grade ω, and"
390..453 Comment "// each read of it copies. The grades are those of graded modal"
454..528 Comment "// types (Orchard, Liepelt and Eades, \"Quantitative program reasoning with"
529..564 Comment "// graded modal types\", ICFP 2019)."
566..641 Comment "// The successor, a call whose type synthesises where a statement binds it."
